 "a_disagreement_names_two_suspects": "A row that disagrees says the reading and the pathway vocabulary are inconsistent; it does not say which is wrong. Opicapone is a nitrocatechol and one of its rows is called Reduction, which this vocabulary takes to be the addition of two hydrogens and which for a nitro group is not: the observed change there is the loss of one oxygen, and the drawing may well be right. The vocabulary is deliberately left as it was written, before any row was checked, because repairing the entries that disagree is how a held-out check stops being one.",
 "reading": "A row that agrees was rebuilt into a molecule whose formula moved by exactly what the document says happened to it, which nothing in the reconstructor could have arranged. A row that disagrees names a drawing feature read wrongly. The rows that are not checked are not failures and not passes: the name states no size, or the drawing marks a region rather than a structure."
